1
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:08,950
Every team meeting starts with ideas and ends with decisions.

2
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:12,850
And a few hours later, we're all asking the same questions.

3
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:15,100
What did we actually decide?

4
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:16,600
Who's responsible?

5
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:19,300
And did that work ever make it into the code?

6
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:32,900
That's why we built Kaam Ki Baat.

7
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:38,000
It connects our conversations from Wispr Flow with actual GitHub code,

8
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:41,500
and uses Bolna to make that entire context conversational.

9
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:43,750
And here's the interesting part.

10
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:46,650
Look left to remember what your team discussed.

11
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:49,650
Look straight to access the leader's private agent,

12
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:53,050
and look right to navigate the actual codebase.

13
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,250
Okay, so let me show you how this actually works.

14
00:01:05,550 --> 00:01:06,950
I'm turning left…

15
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,150
Team Memory activates.

16
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:14,700
It uses the Wispr Flow MCP and understands

17
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:20,350
the meeting context — everything that was talked about in the meeting.

18
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:24,050
I can ask it a question from the meeting,

19
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:27,250
or if something hasn't been finalized, we don't have to guess.

20
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:31,300
We can get that verified directly by our leader — by moving to the center.

21
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:40,000
Now here's my favourite part.

22
00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:45,800
I need to implement and write code — through an AI agent or by myself.

23
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:48,950
I turn right and go to the Code Navigator.

24
00:01:49,050 --> 00:01:51,800
I ask it: show me exactly where this decision

25
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:54,300
is saved in our code, and how we can verify it —

26
00:01:54,350 --> 00:01:58,300
how to implement our next feature, and improve the task.

27
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:21,550
So instead of searching through meetings, messages and hundreds of lines of code,

28
00:02:21,550 --> 00:02:25,200
we know what was decided, where to look, and what to do next.

29
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,850
That's Kaam Ki Baat.

30
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:28,450
Meeting mein bola. Repo mein bana.
